WEBVTT

00:28:26.505 --> 00:28:31.322
And again, in the wake of preparing
to sort of think about this interview

00:28:31.346 --> 00:28:32.874
where I'm a little bit nervous,

00:28:32.898 --> 00:28:36.226
I could actually feel
my stress level go down

00:28:36.250 --> 00:28:39.980
as I got that sort of affirmation,

00:28:40.004 --> 00:28:44.786
that I am a person worth seeing
and trying to help in that moment.

00:28:44.810 --> 00:28:47.411
AG: After seeing the impact
of high-quality connections

00:28:47.435 --> 00:28:48.589
on our work lives,

00:28:48.613 --> 00:28:52.036
Jane created an exercise to help people
learn how to build them rapidly.

00:28:52.060 --> 00:28:55.406
JD: Oh -- I love this exercise.
This is my killer exercise.

00:28:55.430 --> 00:28:58.126
AG: It's something you can do
in almost any work setting.

00:28:58.150 --> 00:29:01.945
You gather a group of people, ideally
from different parts of your organization,